title:: CaosMIDI
summary:: MIDI infrastructure: devices, connections, output wrappers and monitor.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosMIDIOut, Classes/MIDIOut, Classes/MIDIIn

description::
CaosMIDI is the MIDI infrastructure layer. It initializes the MIDI client,
lists the external inputs and outputs, connects devices and creates
link::Classes/CaosMIDIOut:: wrappers. It does not know about tracks, instruments
or the GUI.

By default code::start:: does not connect any input: select one device, or use
code::connectAll:: when there is only one controller. If MIDI is unavailable,
code::start:: posts a warning and returns instead of stopping CaosBox.

The legacy XSession mapping still lives in code::CB/CaosBox-midi.scd:: while the
configurable mapping layer is developed. That script calls
code::CaosMIDI.start(autoConnect: true):: to preserve the current startup.

classmethods::

method:: start
Initializes the MIDI client. With code::autoConnect: true:: it also connects all
inputs.
code::
CaosMIDI.start;                    // init, no input connected
CaosMIDI.start(autoConnect: true); // legacy XSession bootstrap
::

method:: inputs
method:: destinations
method:: devices
Return the currently available external MIDI endpoints. code::devices:: returns
code::(inputs: ..., destinations: ...)::.
code::
CaosMIDI.devices;
::

method:: connectAll
Connects all external inputs. Useful when there is only one controller.

method:: connect
Connects one input by endpoint, list index, device name or uid. Inputs and
outputs are separate lists; an index is the position inside code::inputs::.
code::
CaosMIDI.connect("USB X-Session");
CaosMIDI.connect(CaosMIDI.inputs[3], 0);
CaosMIDI.connect(3, 0); // input list index 3
::
The second argument is the SuperCollider input port. If the startup already
called code::connectAll::, disconnect first or use code::connectOnly::.

method:: connectOnly
Disconnects every input and connects only the selected device.
code::
CaosMIDI.connectOnly("USB X-Session");
::

method:: disconnectAll
Disconnects all MIDI inputs.

method:: out
Returns a cached link::Classes/CaosMIDIOut:: for a destination and channel. The
destination can be an endpoint, list index, device name or uid. On Linux it
also creates the ALSA/JACK output connection automatically; pass
code::autoConnect: false:: to avoid it.
code::
m = CaosMIDI.out("USB X-Session", 0);
m.noteOn(48, 100);
m.noteOff(48);
::

method:: panic
Sends all-notes-off on every output created through CaosMIDI.

method:: monitor
method:: monitorOff
Simple console monitor for note on/off, CC, program change and bend.
code::
CaosMIDI.monitor(true);
CaosMIDI.monitor(false);
::

method:: free
Stops the monitor, sends panic, disconnects inputs and clears cached outputs.

